@prefix tech: <http://techfusion.example/ontology/v1#> .
@prefix inst: <http://techfusion.example/graph/techfusion_graph_demo/> .

#################################################################
# Fixtures for scripts/ontology_demo.py --demo owl ONLY. Never loaded alongside
# the main instance data (they would pollute every other demo's result
# counts). Each one exists to trigger exactly one specific OWL-RL
# entailment or consistency check, discussed in docs/ontology.md section 5.
#################################################################

# --- Fixture 1: owl:FunctionalProperty forcing owl:sameAs -----------
# tech:ownedBy is owl:FunctionalProperty. Asserting two different
# OWNED_BY-shaped triples for the same service is something Cypher
# would happily store as two ordinary edges with no contradiction and
# no inference at all. Under OWL-RL semantics, a functional property's
# object is logically unique, so a reasoner is entitled to infer that
# the two named objects denote the SAME individual.

inst:service-billing-api
    a tech:Service ;
    tech:name "Billing API" .

inst:team-billing-ops
    a tech:Team ;
    tech:name "Billing Ops" .

inst:team-finance-platform
    a tech:Team ;
    tech:name "Finance Platform" .

inst:service-billing-api tech:ownedBy inst:team-billing-ops .
inst:service-billing-api tech:ownedBy inst:team-finance-platform .

# --- Fixture 2: disjoint-class inconsistency ------------------------
# tech:Service owl:disjointWith tech:Team. No reasoner is required to
# "notice" this is wrong by itself (OWL-RL's standard rule set does not
# derive owl:Nothing membership from disjointWith the way a full OWL DL
# reasoner's consistency check would); the demo instead runs a bounded
# SPARQL ASK query over the ontology's own disjointWith axioms plus the
# data's asserted types, which is the practical, lightweight way to
# catch this without standing up a full DL reasoner. See docs/ontology.md section
# 5's "OWL ontology vs database schema" discussion for why this still
# counts as real OWL semantics (disjointWith is itself an OWL axiom;
# only the *mechanism used to check it* here is a SPARQL query rather
# than a DL reasoner's inconsistency proof).

inst:service-dual-typed-anomaly
    a tech:Service, tech:Team ;
    tech:name "Deliberately mistyped node" .
